WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.760
Don't miss that brightly shining light!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.870
It's always there beside you.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:26.420
I'm sure the rest just depends on your perception.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.590
You don't have to search for it—just notice that it's there!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.350
There's a tenderness that lies hidden behind the most common things:

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:43.230
a light that showers our days in color!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.230
Tiny Days: This world is constructed...

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.800
Tiny Days: ...by fragments of miracles!

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.180
Things that seemed meaningless

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.730
were actually protecting us, loving us, more than we ever knew.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.960
Tiny Heart: Our feelings flow forth...

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Tiny Heart: ...as we give thanks for everything we've been given.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.490
We'll never, ever forget...

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.700
We'll cherish this feeling forevermore!

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.000
Hot Pot Day

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:41.760
"When winter comes...

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.430
a single hot pot shall suffice."
a single hotpot shall suffice.
When winter comes...

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.220
Yeah, I totally get it!

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.390
Who said that?

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.020
The building manager put it in with the pot.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.480
The guy's a bit of a mystery, huh?

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.020
Still, he's quite helpful.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:59.360
And Ni-taro was a big help when we were doing our rooms!

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.890
I'm assuming we'll have both the brains and the innards.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.660
Whoa, wait, what are you talking about?!

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.580
About the hot pot. And that means...

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.330
Innards, of course.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.620
That light shade of pink...
That plump, firm flesh...

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:19.320
Hoisting it out, slicing it up,
and seeing those generous organs...

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.470
Anglerfish hot pot is the best!
Offal hot pot is the best!

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.390
Wait, hot pot <i>has</i> to be with offal, don't you think?

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.220
Goodness, no. It has to be with anglerfish.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.500
What are you saying?

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.430
Hot pot must, of course, be in the Yanagawa style!

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.480
"Yanagawa"? What kind of dish is that again?

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.650
Acquisition Mode: "Yanagawa hot pot."

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.090
Data acquisition complete.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:46.110
Yanagawa hot pot has flat-sliced pond loach placed atop shaved burdock root in a circular pattern,

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:51.600
and is flavored with dashi broth, soy sauce, and sugar, with whipped egg poured in.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.160
Well? <i>That</i> is the flavor of Japan, a tradition since the Edo era!

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.980
There's no way one wouldn't eat that!

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.090
Oh, get off your high horse.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.570
It's not like you invented it or anything.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.340
Huh? Wait, isn't there a clam hot pot or something too?

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.840
You fool! You mean Fukagawa-style hot pot!

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:09.850
Acquisition Mode: "Fukagawa-style hot pot."

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:11.350
Data acquisition complete.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:15.350
The main ingredient in Fukagawa-style hot pot is littleneck clams.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:20.380
It is named after the Fukagawa area of Koto City, Tokyo, from which these clams are farmed.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:24.280
Nah, I'd say they just couldn't get their hands on enough fish...

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:26.150
I quite like the loach when it's alive and writhing...

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:27.060
Indeed.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.520
Nothing beats having someone bound and unable to move offered as a sacrifice to the loach.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.410
Give a loach even the slightest opening and it will find its way in...

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:36.160
No!

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.580
You perverts!

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.370
Oh, my. Why are you blushing?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.170
Have you imagined something unseemly?

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.410
What do you mean, "unseemly"?!

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:46.670
Who's to say...?

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.250
Perhaps that's a question to ask your own body.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.600
Forget that!
Maybe we should do a hot pot with more, like, <i>normal</i> ingredients.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.850
What a shame...
Maybe we should do a hot pot with more, like, <i>normal</i> ingredients.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.810
Maybe we should do a hot pot with more, like, <i>normal</i> ingredients.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.270
I've got it! How about a tomato hot pot?

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:58.270
"Tomato hot pot"?

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:02.010
Oh, I heard about that from a girl in my class.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.780
Yup! Girls just love tomato hot pot!

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:09.280
Lycopene is good for the skin,
and the dish has lots of cheese.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.950
To finish, you can add pasta or risotto.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.990
Well? Sounds great, right?

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.450
Huh? What kind of reaction is that?

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.500
Well, tomato hot pot is so...

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.130
It's only become popular in the last few years.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.670
Tomatoes and cheese?

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:29.510
Such pedestrian ingredients in a hot pot is just...

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.840
No way.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.220
What's more, using the broth to add...

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.140
...pasta...

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:34.180
...or risotto!

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:38.540
What's the big idea? Why are you laughing?!

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.650
Base, what kind of hot pot do you like?

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.360
I like sukiyaki!

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:43.880
Gourai, what about you?

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.890
I prefer oden.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.360
Oh...

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.400
Is something wrong?

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:54.140
I was just thinking, I wonder if oden or sukiyaki even count as a hot pot...

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.120
Cooking proteins in a clay pot can cause the pot to break.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.900
Using a metal pot is more highly recommended.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.860
Yeah, you're right. So I guess sukiyaki is out.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:04.650
Yay!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.670
What about oden?

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.010
"Oden" is a common name for ingredients that have been simmered in broth.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.470
It originated as a dish of skewered tofu in grilled miso.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.270
Its current form of ingredients seeped in fish broth has its origins in the Edo era.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:22.380
Wow! So it wasn't technically a hot pot dish!

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.060
The Edo period? Excellent!

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.940
Then it's a relative of Yanagawa-style hot pot!

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:29.940
Jinrai, what is it with you and your obsession with the Edo period?

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.250
She just likes old stuff!

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.320
Speaking of, you like sumo as well, right?

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.400
traditional sumo wrestler dish
Do you also like chanko hot pot?

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.410
Ch... Chanko hot pot?

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:44.540
Unless made by fighters of the sumo ring,
it is but a pale imitation!

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.790
You give up a bit too soon, don't you, Jinrai-chan?

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:48.590
What?

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:51.420
We'll have Ao-chan feed you lots of rice...

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.180
Get you nice and fat...

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:56.010
Should I be made to join a sumo stable...!

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.010
Dosukoi!

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.460
Forget it, no way!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:02.790
Still, this is a problem.
What sort of hot pot should we do?

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:06.020
Why not just throw a bunch of stuff in some broth and let it simmer?

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.860
That's how we've always done it.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:14.240
We'd do it in a seaweed broth, then everyone in our family would dip stuff in their favorite sauce.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:19.560
In that case, choosing which ingredients to cook is important, isn't it?

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:23.070
Sure is! Okay, I better go right now and...

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.840
What is it, Ao?

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:32.200
I've already burned through this month's food budget.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.430
I'm sure we had eggs, though.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.200
And you still have rice.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.960
Just eggs and rice...?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.520
Learning Mode: "Egg and rice recipes."

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.960
Data acquisition complete.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.760
Possible recipe: Rice gruel.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.650
That's what you add after everything else is gone!

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.160
I know!

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.320
Why not ask the building manager for something?

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.610
That's a nice idea!

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.440
I'm sure he'd give you something delicious!

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.060
I-I don't know...

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.950
Go get some anglerfish, Ao!

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.570
Ask him for some loach.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.450
Yeah, there's no way he'd have that...

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.550
Uh, sorry. Um...

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.650
What? All this?

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.650
And you even have loach?!

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:16.010
I totally can't believe it,
but the manager had everything.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.340
He really is a mystery...

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.760
Still, he's awesome!

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.660
Well then, shall we begin?

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.140
Huh? Begin what?

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:24.380
Well...

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.480
The Tale of 100 Hot Pots.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.980
"The Tale of 100 Hot Pots"?

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.840
Data acquisition complete.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.860
The Tale of 100 Hot Pots is a family game,

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:38.720
the rule for which is that each person can add an ingredient for a hot pot related story they tell.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.740
Where did you get that "data" from?!

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:44.080
This information of yours is getting shadier by the minute!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.960
Okay, I guess I'll start...

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.080
Ao, you're buying into this?!

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:51.290
Well, I just really want to start making this hot pot already...

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.250
Yes, that's understandable.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.340
F.A. Girl!

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.210
Ahem!

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:57.840
So, the lids on hot pots have holes in them, right?

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.080
That's because...

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:05.350
when you put the lids on,
the steam inside will rise and make the lid move,

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:10.520
so the hole is there on purpose,
to let the steam out and stop that from happening.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:11.590
Whoa!

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.730
Okay! First ingredient goes in!

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:16.640
The clay hot pot is well suited to cooking rice porridge.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.900
What? Really?!

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:22.390
The starch in the rice porridge seeps within the cracks of the pot, thus preventing water drainage.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:25.540
Huh? So then, maybe we should have started with a rice dish?

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.710
Understood. Inserting white rice.

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:29.210
Whoa, stop, wait!

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:31.430
Oh no! Now it's just rice soup!

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:32.880
Who's next? Someone!

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.090
Did you know? Eating a hot pot dish with someone...

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:37.800
...makes it easier to control them.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.130
Wow, really?

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:42.520
You can have the other person make the whole dish, while you do nothing at all.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:45.810
Meanwhile, the other person acquiesces without even being aware of it,

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.380
thus giving you the psychological advantage.

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:52.980
My hot pot has tomatoes and-

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:57.800
Yes, yes. My hot pot story is, well... Um...

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.790
Hot pot makes the body nice and warm!

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.280
Adding ginger provides additional warmth!

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:06.480
Ginger is quite good for your health, isn't it?

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.900
Wait a minute! I wasn't done talking about my tomato-!

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.650
Done!

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.420
We should lower the heat before the ingredients all simmer down.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:19.170
Um, where's the pot stand?

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:20.420
Ah, there it is.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.300
Okay, let's eat!

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:26.510
Wait, come to think of it...

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:29.020
Gourai, you and the others can't eat this, can you?

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:30.670
Yes, you're correct.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:31.890
I know, right?

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:34.270
Wait, so I have to eat all this myself?

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.560
What?!

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.900
You can do it, Ao!
We're rooting for you!

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:38.840
Uh, okay...

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:41.110
I guess that means we've got some free time, huh?

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:44.180
Very well! In that case, what do you say to a battle?

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:44.980
A battle?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.450
Yes! I believe I'd like to ask Gourai-kai for a rematch!

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.310
Yeah, sounds good.

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:53.330
Go make me some money for the food budget...

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:55.030
I challenge you, Gourai!

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.590
Sure, that's fine by me!

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:58.380
F.A. Girl!

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:01.830
What ails you, Charger-kun?

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.590
They're looking for something!

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:06.180
It looks like they can't find the Session Base.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:06.830
What?

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:09.060
Wait! Has it honestly disappeared?!

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:10.720
Maybe it's under the bed.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:11.850
Inconceivable!

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:13.770
Maybe it just got misplaced.

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:16.110
It would not be treated so carelessly!

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:18.850
Maybe it was mistaken for garbage and tossed out...

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:23.860
Living our lives as Frame Arms Girls without battling would be both pitiable and wonderful, no?

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:27.200
Don't tell me one of you peons has hidden it!

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:30.370
What is the meaning of those smiles?!

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:33.830
Well, your face is so amusing when you're flustered.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.080
What was that?!

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:37.400
It's totally, really gone, huh?

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.670
Jinrai-chan, your switch gets so easily flipped, doesn't it?

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:42.760
Sure enough, one of you peasants is behind this!

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:45.410
Come on, Jinrai! Calm down!

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.410
Confess, Materia siblings!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.930
Cease this subterfuge!

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:54.920
Well, it's fine.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:01.690
What's the matter, Gourai?

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:06.840
It's something you said earlier,
about that object with the hole...

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.330
Oh, you mean lid on the hot pot?

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.520
Yes. But what is this feeling...?

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.870
Ah! Maybe you're finding something in common!

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:15.660
What?

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:20.750
Could it be you think you're lacking something that other people have?

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:27.380
If being a Frame Arms Girl means you don't know much about emotions...

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.300
Well, that's something that's important to you, right?

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:32.630
And you lack it <i>because</i> it's important.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:35.880
Lacking because it's important...

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:42.020
Yup! Learning about emotions can teach you about a lot of other things, right?

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.890
It's because you lack them that you get to experience those other things.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.140
I suppose you're right...

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.410
Hey, Gourai! What are you doing?

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:52.270
Come over here and help me!

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:56.320
Sorry, I'm busy interacting with a companion right now.

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:59.000
Girl, that's a water flea!

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.880
This is unforgiveable!

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.540
Very well: it's come to <i>this!</i>

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:04.590
Why you...!

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.160
Calm down!
Why you...!

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:07.630
Why you...!

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:15.980
Battle! Battle!! Battle!!!
Battle! Battle!! Battle!!!

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:17.890
When winter comes...

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.760
A single hot pot is pitiful indeed.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.400
Oh.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:30.910
Yeah, that's true...

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:33.990
Jinrai-chan just can't get over it, can she?

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:38.270
Still, it's quite the discovery:
using the Session Base as a pot stand...

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.530
Has utterly destroyed her.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.210
The embers have died out...

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:46.080
I-I'm sorry I didn't pay more attention.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:48.050
You need not apologize, Ao.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.380
That's right, Ao!

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:52.220
No one could have noticed under such conditions.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:53.840
Um, yeah.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.460
Actually, I actually <i>did</i> notice though...

00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:59.560
So, what do you say, Architect?

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:03.550
Upon analysis...

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:04.980
Repair is not possible.

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:06.730
Shock!

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:10.510
Ha! She said "shock!" She actually said "shock!"

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.460
Well, fine.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:16.040
We'll just have to send it back to
Factory Advance to get it repaired.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.880
What? That's a waste of time.

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:21.260
You'll all be recalled soon anyway, so what does it matter?

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:22.790
What does that even...

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:23.990
Wait, it's you?!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.670
Hresvelgr!

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:29.490
Yo! Hresvelgr here!

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:34.000
What are you doing just barging into our conversation?!

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.470
That's broken, isn't it?

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:37.850
Yeah, sure is.

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:45.610
I was thinking I'd beat all of you as well once
I've beaten Gourai, but I guess I can't now, huh?

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.430
For your knowledge, I will not be "crushed" again.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.450
You've made some upgrades, right?

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.410
You know about that?

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:01.790
I mean, you battled <i>her</i>, right?

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:04.150
She's nothing like me, though.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:07.360
The data from the battle against Hresvelgr was perfectly replicated.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:12.950
I see... So, you have a direct pipeline to the battle data that gets sent to the company, do you?

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.470
That's pretty much it!

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:15.640
Huh?

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:19.640
So, you know everything about Gourai-kai?

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.730
Then we're totally at a disadvantage!

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.270
Data notwithstanding...

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:26.300
...Hresvelgr-chan has certainly penetrated us.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:29.840
There is no denying that she knows our tactics.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:33.780
Would it not be best for both parties to put aside their swords?

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.780
Wait, what?

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:39.330
You mean you're not going to fight, Gourai?!

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.560
Well...

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.660
That's way too boring!

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:44.460
I want to fight the new Gourai-kai!

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:47.500
C'mon, let's do it! Let's do this, Gourai!

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.410
Understood. Let's fight.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:59.180
If you're not really up for it then you should do it some other time, Gourai.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.730
The human has a point.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.910
If you fight and your heat isn't really in it,
that would be super boring for me!

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:25.410
What if I did something to this thing?

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:27.280
Would that get you motivated?

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.920
Wait, wait! What do you mean, "something"?!

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:32.380
Well, who's to say?

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:37.040
Please step away from Ao, Hresvelgr.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.450
You feel like fighting now?

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:43.810
Get away from Ao!

00:15:57.610 --> 00:15:59.570
So you've gotten a little more serious, huh?

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:00.950
Charger-kun!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:20.720
Gourai!

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:21.660
Hresvelgr!

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.520
Frame Arms Girl Session...

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:24.560
Bring it!

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:25.470
Go!
Bring it!

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:26.180
Bring it!

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:39.430
Protecting what's important: that is my fight!

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.490
Don't you dare look away.

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:47.810
Look only at me, and then be crushed by me!

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.000
Take this!

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.700
Huh. Not bad.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:07.040
Tee-hee.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:10.320
It would seem she knows everything about Gourai-kai.

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:11.400
Yeah...

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:12.550
This was unexpected.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.700
What are you doing?!

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.700
Gourai-chan is fighting quite well, isn't she?

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:26.020
And here I thought she was just absent-minded...

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:34.570
I've been wondering...
what <i>that</i> was supposed to mean.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:38.200
You'll all be recalled soon anyway, so what does it matter?

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.630
That's true...

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.760
She did say "recalled."

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:43.700
Oh, about that!

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:49.350
If Gourai loses this battle, they're going to stop recording data here with this human.

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:53.050
That means you'll all be recalled to Factory Advance.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.260
Tut-tut. You've left yourself wide open!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.100
B-But that means...

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.820
We won't... be together anymore?

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:03.770
Sure does!

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.440
That's how your system works?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:13.170
There are no clear-cut rules for collection of battle data.

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:16.110
Some believe it's because the necessary data has already been acquired.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:20.170
So that's why Hresvelgr-chan came back, is it?

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:23.040
I'm positively tingling with excitement.

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:25.100
No, I don't like this!

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:26.760
Gourai! You mustn't lose!

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:30.470
Jeez!

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:33.690
You haven't gotten as powerful as I'd expected, Gourai.

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:36.190
I suppose it's because you're in a place like this.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:38.260
A place... like this?

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:42.280
That human activated you by accident, right?

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.020
She's a total amateur.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:47.140
She's useless, and doesn't know a thing about us Frame Arms Girls!

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.500
She's no good to you at all!

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.500
I'm totally getting dissed...

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:53.290
Just go back to the company already.

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:58.420
Get stronger and stronger,
so you can keep on fighting me!

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:08.830
Is that why... you did what you did earlier?

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.080
Huh?

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.600
Is it why you treated Ao as a hostage...

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:16.940
as some sort of object?

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:19.440
Are you actually angry?

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:21.540
Yes.

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:24.950
I believe... this feeling is anger!

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:26.990
Ooh, nice!

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:29.560
Okay, okay! Now I'm fired up!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:32.040
Beryl Smasher!

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.670
What manner of weapon is that?!

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:43.260
It's so big!

00:19:54.750 --> 00:20:00.760
Beryl Smasher: Blaze Tempest Burst!

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:20.960
The breaker went off?

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.300
Are you all okay?

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.550
Jeez, so it's a draw?

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:30.200
Still, it was more fun than I expected!

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.930
Well, you'll be seeing me again. Bye!

00:20:56.950 --> 00:21:01.440
If I lose to her next time, we'll all...

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:14.080
They'll soon show up at your door,

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:19.480
for my special someone, parts of hearts!

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:29.760
Counting the days I can't see you,

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:37.210
I want to hear your voice so badly I feel like crying!

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:40.700
I'm new to this world,

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:44.170
so I lack the language to describe it.

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.440
To knockoffs, say...

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:49.890
"No!" Take care to avoid them.

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:53.410
I want to be be dedicated!

00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:02.110
I want to build it all from nothing!

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:05.340
We laugh and we fight,

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:08.950
creating our unique specs!

00:22:08.950 --> 00:22:14.870
By mixing love and hate,

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:22.940
I want to create more of these funny, carefree days, the parts of Girl!

00:22:40.390 --> 00:22:42.140
When making Yanagawa hot pot,

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:46.230
it's important to make sure the charger area doesn't get clogged, isn't it?

00:22:46.230 --> 00:22:46.960
Just thinking about that was enough to make me go "Gaaaah!"

00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:49.230
A Public Bath! A Battle?!
What Lies Behind That Emotion

00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:51.690
Next time on Frame Arms Girl, let's have...

00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:53.360
...another session together. There it goes...

00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:54.890
Gaaaah!

00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:54.990
What Lies Behind That Emotion
